Conda channel (https://conda.ikafssn.org; runtime deps from conda-forge):

  Subdirs available: linux-64, linux-aarch64, osx-arm64

  Runtime packages (pulled from conda-forge during install):
    tbb
    lmdb
    libsqlite
    libcurl
    jsoncpp
    openssl
    libuuid  (linux only; osx-arm64 uses libSystem)
    zlib
    bzip2
    xz
    zstd
    libdeflate

  Linux baseline: glibc 2.34 (RHEL 9 / Ubuntu 22.04 / Debian 12 and newer).
  osx-arm64 baseline: macOS 11.

  The channel itself only hosts repodata.json index files (CEP-15
  base_url); the .conda binaries are served from ikafssn's
  GitHub Releases.

  Client requirements: conda 23.7+ or micromamba 2.0+ (for base_url).

APT channel (https://deb.ikafssn.org; .deb hosted in-channel):

  Suites available:
    noble   Ubuntu 24.04 LTS
  Architectures: amd64, arm64

  Runtime dependencies match the corresponding Ubuntu .deb variant
  above (libtbb12 / liblmdb0 / ... ); dpkg resolves them from the
  distribution's own archives at install time.

  Client requirements: apt, curl, gnupg.
  Signing: GPG-signed Release / InRelease / Release.gpg per suite,
  verified by apt against the channel's public key.

DNF channel (https://rpm.ikafssn.org; .rpm hosted in-channel):

  releasevers available:
    9    AlmaLinux / Rocky Linux / RHEL 9
    10   AlmaLinux / Rocky Linux / RHEL 10
  Architectures: x86_64, aarch64

  Runtime dependencies match the corresponding EL .rpm variant above
  (tbb / lmdb-libs / ... ); dnf resolves them from the distribution's
  own repositories at install time.

  Client requirements: dnf.
  Signing: each .rpm is re-signed with rpm --addsign, and repomd.xml
  carries a detached GPG signature. Both gpgcheck=1 and
  repo_gpgcheck=1 in the .repo file are verified against the
  channel's public key.

Build dependencies (from source)
----------------------------------

Compiler and tools:

  C++20 compiler (GCC >= 13 or Clang >= 15)

  The NCBI C++ Toolkit 30.7.0 build refuses anything older than GCC 13.
  CMake >= 3.16

System packages — Ubuntu 24.04 / 26.04 (x86_64 / aarch64):

  build-essential cmake pkg-config
  libtbb-dev liblmdb-dev libsqlite3-dev
  libcurl4-openssl-dev libjsoncpp-dev
  zlib1g-dev libbz2-dev liblzma-dev libzstd-dev libdeflate-dev autoconf
  libssl-dev uuid-dev

  libssl-dev and uuid-dev are required for building the NCBI C++ Toolkit
  and Drogon from source. With -DBUILD_HTTPD=OFF, uuid-dev becomes
  optional.

System packages — EL 9 / EL 10 (x86_64 / aarch64):

  gcc-c++ cmake make pkgconfig
  tbb-devel lmdb-devel sqlite-devel
  libcurl-devel jsoncpp-devel
  zlib-devel bzip2-devel xz-devel libzstd-devel libdeflate-devel
  openssl-devel libuuid-devel
  autoconf automake libtool

  Requires: epel-release and CRB (CodeReady Builder) repository enabled.
  With -DBUILD_HTTPD=OFF, libuuid-devel becomes optional.

System packages — macOS (Homebrew):

  cmake pkg-config tbb lmdb sqlite3 curl jsoncpp
  xz zstd libdeflate autoconf automake libtool openssl@3

  openssl@3 is required for both the NCBI C++ Toolkit and Drogon source
  builds. uuid is provided by libSystem.

Conda packaging (recipe/, conda-forge channel):

  Build environment:
    {{ compiler('c') }} {{ compiler('cxx') }} {{ stdlib('c') }}
    cmake make autoconf automake libtool patch curl pkg-config

  Host environment:
    tbb-devel lmdb libsqlite libcurl jsoncpp openssl
    libuuid (linux only) zlib bzip2 xz zstd libdeflate

  Linux baseline: c_stdlib_version 2.34 (sysroot_linux-{64,aarch64}).
  osx-arm64 baseline: MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET 11.0.

Source-built libraries:

  NCBI C++ Toolkit 30.7.0  — BLAST DB access (CSeqDB::SetMMapStrategy, upstream since 30.7.0)
  Parasail 2.6.2           — Stage 3 pairwise alignment
  htslib 1.24            — SAM/BAM output
  Drogon 1.9.13            — HTTP framework for ikafssnhttpd
                             (static, with trantor 1.5.28 placed at
                             drogon-1.9.13/trantor; ORM/brotli/yaml-cpp/
                             drogon_ctl/examples/docs disabled)
